4) MINIMUM INSERTIONS / DELETIONS TO CONVERT STRING A TO STRING B

🔥 Very frequently asked

Appears in Amazon, Infosys, TCS Prime, Accenture

DP + LCS

Tests string DP fundamentals

📌 Problem Statement

Given two strings A and B, find:

Minimum number of deletions

Minimum number of insertions

required to convert string A into string B.

❗Replacement is NOT allowed

✍ Example
A = "heap"
B = "pea"
Output:
Deletions = 2
Insertions = 1

🧠 Key Insight (INTERVIEW GOLD)

The Longest Common Subsequence (LCS) of A and B determines the minimum operations.

🧮 Formula

Let:

L = LCS(A, B)


Then:

Deletions  = length(A) - L
Insertions = length(B) - L

📐 Algorithm

Compute LCS(A, B) using DP

Use formulas to calculate deletions & insertions

💻 Java Code
public class MinInsertDelete {

    public static void minOperations(String A, String B) {

        int n = A.length();
        int m = B.length();

        int[][] dp = new int[n + 1][m + 1];

        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {

                if (A.charAt(i - 1) == B.charAt(j - 1)) {
                    dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i - 1][j - 1];
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
                }
            }
        }

        int lcs = dp[n][m];

        int deletions = n - lcs;
        int insertions = m - lcs;

        System.out.println("Deletions: " + deletions);
        System.out.println("Insertions: " + insertions);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String A = "heap";
        String B = "pea";
        minOperations(A, B);
    }
}

